WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.700
- I think I'm depressed.

00:00:01.700 --> 00:00:02.533
- Yeah?

00:00:02.533 --> 00:00:04.810
- It started when I was
having trouble with my book

00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:08.590
and then it kind of snowballed
into my boyfriend saying

00:00:08.590 --> 00:00:10.196
I should take antidepressants.

00:00:10.196 --> 00:00:11.267
- Are you going to?

00:00:11.267 --> 00:00:12.131
- What's the point?

00:00:12.131 --> 00:00:13.305
- Of antidepressants?

00:00:13.305 --> 00:00:15.280
I believe the point is
to be anti-depressed.

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:18.480
- Sure or you just flip over the nothing

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:21.357
and underneath there's more nothing.

00:00:21.357 --> 00:00:24.524
(lively guitar music)

00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:31.420
- [Dan] Over six seasons, BoJack Horseman,

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:32.900
has delivered a groundbreaking,

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:36.030
nuanced exploration of mental health.

00:00:36.030 --> 00:00:39.140
It has subverted expectations
around animated shows

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:43.020
and sitcom structure to deliver
a single, narrative arc,

00:00:43.020 --> 00:00:46.740
exploring not just the reality
of living with mental illness

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:49.170
but also examining it's many root causes

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:50.570
and knock on effects.

00:00:50.570 --> 00:00:51.660
- I can't keep lying to myself,

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:53.613
saying I'm gonna change, I'm poison.

00:00:53.613 --> 00:00:54.446
- BoJack.

00:00:54.446 --> 00:00:56.830
- I come from poison,
I have poison inside me

00:00:56.830 --> 00:00:58.374
and I destroy everything I touch.

00:00:58.374 --> 00:01:00.010
That's my legacy.

00:01:00.010 --> 00:01:01.210
- [Dan] In BoJack Horseman,

00:01:01.210 --> 00:01:04.360
the world doesn't reset at
the end of every episode

00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:09.360
and as such, every action sooner
or later has a consequence.

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:13.600
- So you don't know where
Sarah Lynn got the heroin from?

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:14.440
- I have no idea.

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:17.370
- Alrighty then, that's
the only question I had.

00:01:17.370 --> 00:01:20.020
- I mean, of course, I knew
she was doing a lot of drugs,

00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:22.210
but that's who she was, who I was.

00:01:22.210 --> 00:01:24.120
Felt like we could keep partying forever

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:25.450
and it wouldn't catch up with us.

00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:27.480
- [Dan] In the first
few seasons the camera

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:30.010
was fixed firmly on BoJack himself.

00:01:30.010 --> 00:01:32.960
A middle aged, fading star,
suffering the twin perils

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:35.080
of addiction and depression.

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:39.210
The cycles of which he found
himself unable to escape.

00:01:39.210 --> 00:01:41.350
- [BoJack] You stupid alcoholic,
talk to your daughter.

00:01:41.350 --> 00:01:43.010
You're ruining her, you know that, right?

00:01:43.010 --> 00:01:44.810
No matter what, your
poison is already in her,

00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:45.860
there's nothing you can do.

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:46.693
That's not true.

00:01:46.693 --> 00:01:48.270
Yeah, it is, you stupid piece of shit.

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:49.820
You're a real stupid piece of shit

00:01:49.820 --> 00:01:52.400
and everywhere you go, you destroy people.

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:54.090
- [Dan] But in recent seasons,

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:56.410
the lens has shifted somewhat.

00:01:56.410 --> 00:02:00.230
Zoomed out, expanding the
scope of the stories being told

00:02:00.230 --> 00:02:04.620
and giving us a broader view
of depression, anxiety, PTSD

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:05.730
and dementia.

00:02:05.730 --> 00:02:07.929
Attempting to document the many masks

00:02:07.929 --> 00:02:09.943
that mental illness wears.

00:02:11.270 --> 00:02:13.680
- Okay, yeah, I've been a
little depressed but I'm not,

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:16.770
like, depressed, I don't have depression.

00:02:16.770 --> 00:02:19.570
- [Dan] By spending time with
the supporting characters

00:02:19.570 --> 00:02:22.420
and showing us more of the
struggles they're dealing with,

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:26.680
season six, as a whole, and
episode seven in particular

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:28.020
is dispelling the myth

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:31.120
that mental illness only
affects certain people

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:32.883
and deconstructing the question,

00:02:32.883 --> 00:02:34.823
what does depression look like?

00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:38.030
- What is depression?

00:02:38.030 --> 00:02:38.863
- Depression.

00:02:38.863 --> 00:02:40.650
- Who is depression?

00:02:40.650 --> 00:02:42.970
- You or someone you love.

00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:44.940
- Where is depression?

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:46.820
- A grassy field, perhaps.

00:02:46.820 --> 00:02:50.110
- If any of these words
describe you or your feelings,

00:02:50.110 --> 00:02:51.850
you may suffer from.

00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:53.017
- Depression.
- Depression.

00:02:53.017 --> 00:02:55.200
(somber music)

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:58.320
- [Dan] In episode seven,
BoJack, fresh out of rehab

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:00.110
and on a mission to make amends,

00:03:00.110 --> 00:03:01.720
travels the country checking in with

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:04.240
his now disparate friends and loved ones.

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:06.010
- So what're you gonna do now?

00:03:06.010 --> 00:03:07.880
Just keep getting lunch with your friends?

00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:09.470
- There was a stewardess in the meeting,

00:03:09.470 --> 00:03:11.510
she was talking about
how everyday she wakes up

00:03:11.510 --> 00:03:13.030
in a different place.

00:03:13.030 --> 00:03:15.150
I thought, that sounds perfect.

00:03:15.150 --> 00:03:17.000
Every city, a clean slate.

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:18.110
- Stewardess?

00:03:18.110 --> 00:03:21.710
I think the preferred
term is flight servant.

00:03:21.710 --> 00:03:23.600
- [Dan] Throughout season six, BoJack,

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:25.700
has been working through the 12 steps

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:29.050
and struggling with both
reality and his identity.

00:03:29.050 --> 00:03:33.310
Now he's sober, if he doesn't
hate himself then who is he?

00:03:33.310 --> 00:03:36.910
- Of course, you did this to
me, because I cared about you

00:03:36.910 --> 00:03:39.223
and you ruin people who care about you.

00:03:40.690 --> 00:03:41.800
- Well, best of luck.

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:44.223
- I want you to remember this, BoJack.

00:03:44.223 --> 00:03:46.341
I want you to remember what you did to me.

00:03:46.341 --> 00:03:48.310
(forlorn music)

00:03:48.310 --> 00:03:49.510
- I remember everything.

00:03:50.345 --> 00:03:52.210
I'm sober now.

00:03:52.210 --> 00:03:54.130
- [Dan] We followed him
through chemical highs

00:03:54.130 --> 00:03:57.340
and ever lower lows but against
the odds, by this episode,

00:03:57.340 --> 00:03:59.640
BoJack is finally making good choices.

00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:01.890
While those around him
are seeming to stumble,

00:04:01.890 --> 00:04:04.784
he is the one who has made the
most progress towards balance

00:04:04.784 --> 00:04:06.510
and wellness.

00:04:06.510 --> 00:04:07.780
- Okay, you got me.

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:10.650
My parents gave me an
internalized self hatred of horses

00:04:10.650 --> 00:04:13.460
so my horse body is a prison
that I can never escape.

00:04:13.460 --> 00:04:15.080
This manifests in rotten behavior

00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:16.500
because I subconsciously believe

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:18.510
I deserve to be punished but being famous,

00:04:18.510 --> 00:04:20.670
I'm never punished so I act out even more

00:04:20.670 --> 00:04:23.410
and since this pattern is
so woven into my identity

00:04:23.410 --> 00:04:26.160
it is unfathomable to me
that it can ever be curbed

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:28.340
so instead I drink!

00:04:28.340 --> 00:04:29.173
- Check, please!

00:04:29.173 --> 00:04:31.120
- So the only way I can
progress is to return

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:32.250
to my life as a sober man

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:34.560
and finally hold myself
accountable for my actions,

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:35.450
past and future.

00:04:35.450 --> 00:04:37.930
Oh, my God, is this what therapy is?

00:04:37.930 --> 00:04:39.830
- [Dan] His friends are in pain.

00:04:39.830 --> 00:04:41.230
Each at a crossroads.

00:04:41.230 --> 00:04:45.950
Transitioning between life
stages, jobs and relationships.

00:04:45.950 --> 00:04:48.870
- It's so amazing to hold
a baby and look at it sleep

00:04:48.870 --> 00:04:51.640
and think, this is a perfect thing.

00:04:51.640 --> 00:04:52.473
- I can't imagine.

00:04:52.473 --> 00:04:55.413
- It's weird to think that at
one point someone held me in

00:04:55.413 --> 00:04:57.210
their hands and thought,

00:04:57.210 --> 00:05:00.440
I'm going to love this
kid forever, you know?

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:01.273
What happened?

00:05:01.273 --> 00:05:02.490
- What happened to what?

00:05:02.490 --> 00:05:03.360
- I dunno.

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:05.350
Moms are weird, right?

00:05:05.350 --> 00:05:06.183
- Yeah.

00:05:06.183 --> 00:05:08.830
- [Dan] BoJack has no
answers but he's present.

00:05:08.830 --> 00:05:11.920
For the first time in a
long time, he's turning up.

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:14.060
He's a terrible listener but he's trying.

00:05:14.060 --> 00:05:15.400
- I need my job!

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:16.620
I love my job!

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:17.453
- Okay!

00:05:17.453 --> 00:05:19.570
- It's just, there's always
so much stupid bullshit

00:05:19.570 --> 00:05:20.630
to take care of there.

00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:21.670
- Aren't you the boss?

00:05:21.670 --> 00:05:23.133
Why are you doing the stupid bullshit?

00:05:23.133 --> 00:05:23.980
- I dunno.

00:05:23.980 --> 00:05:26.890
- Hey, my only responsibility
right now is to not drink

00:05:26.890 --> 00:05:28.160
and I'm barely getting by.

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:31.200
You are producing a
show, running a company,

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:34.290
catering to your clients,
raising a child, a tod,

00:05:34.290 --> 00:05:36.870
you need your own Princess
Carolyn to take care of you.

00:05:36.870 --> 00:05:39.112
- [Dan] And though he does offer comfort,

00:05:39.112 --> 00:05:43.560
he realizes during these visits
that he can only do so much.

00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:46.570
The ripples of his self
destruction spread further

00:05:46.570 --> 00:05:48.700
than simple words can reach.

00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:51.660
- I was in a bad way and
Sarah Lynn followed me down

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:55.170
because she thought I was a safe place.

00:05:55.170 --> 00:05:56.090
What have I done?

00:05:56.090 --> 00:05:57.950
- [Dan] The one friend BoJack can help

00:05:57.950 --> 00:06:01.240
is the only one who isn't
struggling, Mr. Peanutbutter,

00:06:01.240 --> 00:06:03.690
a pathologically happy yellow lab,

00:06:03.690 --> 00:06:07.000
is being publicly vilified
for cheating on his fiance

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:09.241
until Princess Carolyn convinces the world

00:06:09.241 --> 00:06:11.210
that he's depressed.

00:06:11.210 --> 00:06:13.120
He's called a hero for speaking up

00:06:13.120 --> 00:06:16.660
and is named the national
face of depression.

00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:19.733
Mr. Peanutbutter is not
even sure what depression is

00:06:19.733 --> 00:06:22.250
but he's pretty sure he doesn't have it.

00:06:22.250 --> 00:06:23.970
- I am

00:06:23.970 --> 00:06:25.031
not depressed.

00:06:25.031 --> 00:06:25.864
(gasping)

00:06:25.864 --> 00:06:27.360
- Wait, how can you know that?

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:29.620
- Well I feel very happy.

00:06:29.620 --> 00:06:34.070
Oh, I know, just as I
suspected, half full.

00:06:34.070 --> 00:06:35.430
- That is a troubling development.

00:06:35.430 --> 00:06:36.870
- And right before our tour!

00:06:36.870 --> 00:06:39.440
I would be quite upset by
this if I were at all prone

00:06:39.440 --> 00:06:42.300
to depression which as we've
just established, I am not.

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:44.530
- But isn't it possible
that you are depressed

00:06:44.530 --> 00:06:45.440
and just don't know it.

00:06:45.440 --> 00:06:47.980
- Well I do frequently not know things.

00:06:47.980 --> 00:06:49.840
- According to the
literature for this tour

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:52.120
that I did not read, but had my mom peruse

00:06:52.120 --> 00:06:53.270
and then paraphrase for me,

00:06:53.270 --> 00:06:56.810
people who seem happy can
actually be the most depressed.

00:06:56.810 --> 00:06:58.610
- Oh, no, I seem very happy!

00:06:58.610 --> 00:06:59.443
- I know!

00:06:59.443 --> 00:07:01.260
- But, wait, you seem happy too.

00:07:01.260 --> 00:07:03.210
- Oh, no, does that
mean I'm also depressed?

00:07:03.210 --> 00:07:05.190
- Oh, good thing we're going on this tour.

00:07:05.190 --> 00:07:06.590
- We gotta get the word out.

00:07:06.590 --> 00:07:09.400
- [Dan] This is BoJack at it's best.

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:11.270
The very real issues affecting

00:07:11.270 --> 00:07:14.390
Mr. Peanutbutter's friends
and loved ones are made

00:07:14.390 --> 00:07:17.260
a mockery of by his sudden celebrity.

00:07:17.260 --> 00:07:20.830
What the show is doing is
exactly what depression does.

00:07:20.830 --> 00:07:23.080
It undercuts you at every turn.

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:26.120
- You're looking at the
national face of depression.

00:07:26.120 --> 00:07:27.910
- You're the national face of depression?

00:07:27.910 --> 00:07:28.743
- Yup.

00:07:28.743 --> 00:07:29.576
- This face?

00:07:29.576 --> 00:07:30.409
- Uh-huh.

00:07:30.409 --> 00:07:31.340
- You're depressed?

00:07:31.340 --> 00:07:33.630
- [Dan] Literally any other
character in the show would be

00:07:33.630 --> 00:07:35.850
a more suitable face of depression

00:07:35.850 --> 00:07:38.620
but the overwhelmingly
positive, Mr. Peanutbutter,

00:07:38.620 --> 00:07:41.470
is the only face the public will accept.

00:07:41.470 --> 00:07:45.030
Everyone else is, well, too depressing.

00:07:45.030 --> 00:07:47.220
- Well, I gotta say, I am having the time

00:07:47.220 --> 00:07:48.800
of my life being depressed.

00:07:48.800 --> 00:07:50.670
- [Dan] Is this willingness to poke fun

00:07:50.670 --> 00:07:53.010
at the most difficult
aspects of mental health

00:07:53.010 --> 00:07:54.803
that makes BoJack so good.

00:07:55.830 --> 00:07:59.070
The humor helps balance
the dark and the heartfelt

00:07:59.070 --> 00:08:01.690
and ensures that on the
occasions the writers swap

00:08:01.690 --> 00:08:05.490
a complex punchline
for a simple gut punch.

00:08:05.490 --> 00:08:07.967
BoJack is rarely short of devastating.

00:08:07.967 --> 00:08:09.050
- [BoJack Voiceover] The
main thing I think about

00:08:09.050 --> 00:08:11.550
is how stupid I am that
I didn't do this sooner.

00:08:11.550 --> 00:08:13.280
I wasted so many years being miserable

00:08:13.280 --> 00:08:16.313
because I assumed that
was the only way to be.

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:18.660
I don't wanna do that anymore.

00:08:18.660 --> 00:08:20.210
(somber music)

00:08:20.210 --> 00:08:21.213
Also, am I crazy

00:08:21.213 --> 00:08:24.070
or have I gotten really
good at writing letters?

00:08:24.070 --> 00:08:28.080
- [Dan] The road to recovery
isn't just 12 big steps,

00:08:28.080 --> 00:08:30.090
it's 1000 small ones.

00:08:30.090 --> 00:08:31.950
BoJack is making tiny,

00:08:31.950 --> 00:08:36.300
incremental leaps in the right
direction on his journey to

00:08:36.300 --> 00:08:38.690
a destination he may never arrive at.

00:08:38.690 --> 00:08:43.180
Certainly not before the show
ends but that's the struggle.

00:08:43.180 --> 00:08:44.730
For all of us.

00:08:44.730 --> 00:08:47.543
Well, unwell and in between.

00:08:48.380 --> 00:08:52.550
It's the journey and, yes, the
friends we make along the way

00:08:52.550 --> 00:08:53.953
that make it all worthwhile.

00:08:55.730 --> 00:08:57.483
Everyone is struggling.

00:08:58.580 --> 00:09:00.258
None of us are alone.

00:09:00.258 --> 00:09:03.100
(inspirational music)

00:09:03.100 --> 00:09:05.750
- You do this thing where
you don't think you can ever

00:09:05.750 --> 00:09:08.020
be forgiven so you don't apologize

00:09:08.020 --> 00:09:10.860
but I can't forgive you if
you don't say you're sorry.

00:09:10.860 --> 00:09:11.693
- Okay.

00:09:11.693 --> 00:09:13.060
I'm sorry.

00:09:13.060 --> 00:09:13.990
- Thank you.

00:09:13.990 --> 00:09:15.150
That's all I wanted.

00:09:15.150 --> 00:09:15.983
- I'm sorry.

00:09:15.983 --> 00:09:16.816
- I love you.

00:09:16.816 --> 00:09:18.063
- I love you too!

00:09:18.063 --> 00:09:18.896
Come here.

00:09:19.960 --> 00:09:20.793
- That's it?

00:09:20.793 --> 00:09:21.626
- Come on.

00:09:21.626 --> 00:09:23.215
Let's dance.
- Yeah!

00:09:23.215 --> 00:09:24.048
BoJack!

00:09:25.740 --> 00:09:28.540
- [Dan] But creator, Raphael Bob-Waksberg,

00:09:28.540 --> 00:09:32.620
is too savvy to suggest
that BoJack is all better

00:09:32.620 --> 00:09:36.360
or that depression is an
illness that can be cured.

00:09:36.360 --> 00:09:40.320
This show is all about
the ebb and flow of life.

00:09:40.320 --> 00:09:42.490
The natural ups and downs.

00:09:42.490 --> 00:09:45.260
It's about the day
after happily ever after

00:09:45.260 --> 00:09:46.960
and the day after that.

00:09:46.960 --> 00:09:48.757
- [BoJack] So the thing
I keep thinking about is,

00:09:48.757 --> 00:09:51.560
was it worth it for
Beverly to be happy for

00:09:51.560 --> 00:09:54.350
a little bit even though it ended up sad

00:09:54.350 --> 00:09:55.370
or would it have been better

00:09:55.370 --> 00:09:57.150
if the whole thing never happened?

00:09:57.150 --> 00:09:59.360
- [Dan] At the end of
episode seven, BoJack,

00:09:59.360 --> 00:10:02.430
visits a historical reenactment
town where he attends

00:10:02.430 --> 00:10:03.860
a church service.

00:10:03.860 --> 00:10:06.480
- It is only when we show
ourselves forgiveness

00:10:06.480 --> 00:10:08.890
and mercy that we truly
live a life of grace.

00:10:08.890 --> 00:10:10.760
That we are reborn!

00:10:10.760 --> 00:10:13.740
Turn to the horse next to
you and offer a sign of grace

00:10:13.740 --> 00:10:15.908
and peace in the name of the Lord.

00:10:15.908 --> 00:10:16.990
- [Church Goers] Peace, peace be with you.

00:10:16.990 --> 00:10:19.255
- [Dan] He offers
enthusiast affirmations of,

00:10:19.255 --> 00:10:22.910
may peace be with you,
to his fellow patrons

00:10:22.910 --> 00:10:25.490
but peace is not with him,

00:10:25.490 --> 00:10:29.260
not yet, just as he is
attending a facsimile of

00:10:29.260 --> 00:10:32.560
a historical church service,
BoJack feels like he is

00:10:32.560 --> 00:10:35.340
a facsimile of a real person

00:10:35.340 --> 00:10:36.173
or horse.

00:10:37.210 --> 00:10:39.990
He's walking the walk of wellness.

00:10:39.990 --> 00:10:41.750
But it feels pretend.

00:10:41.750 --> 00:10:45.400
The question BoJack is left with, is this,

00:10:45.400 --> 00:10:47.020
when you've spent the better part

00:10:47.020 --> 00:10:50.340
of your adult life wrecking
everything you touch,

00:10:50.340 --> 00:10:53.090
how do you begin to reckon with the ruins?

00:10:53.090 --> 00:10:54.880
- I bought into this
idea that I was the thing

00:10:54.880 --> 00:10:59.200
that couldn't be changed so
the reason I came to Chicago is

00:11:00.230 --> 00:11:04.350
I wanted to thank you for
believing in me when I didn't

00:11:04.350 --> 00:11:07.530
and for encouraging me to
accept the help I needed.

00:11:07.530 --> 00:11:10.940
- [Dan] BoJack's face is the
very face we think of when

00:11:10.940 --> 00:11:12.743
we think of the face of depression.

00:11:13.730 --> 00:11:16.570
When your illness is so
tied to your identity,

00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:19.410
can you ever truly leave
that identity behind?

00:11:19.410 --> 00:11:21.500
And who would you be without it?

00:11:21.500 --> 00:11:24.580
It remains to be seen whether
BoJack can forgive himself

00:11:24.580 --> 00:11:26.220
for the pain he's caused

00:11:26.220 --> 00:11:29.220
or if his forthcoming self-judgment day

00:11:29.220 --> 00:11:32.100
will see him tumble back into
the depths of depression,

00:11:32.100 --> 00:11:34.350
addiction and loneliness.

00:11:34.350 --> 00:11:38.710
Season six started with a
reference to the well known joke.

00:11:38.710 --> 00:11:40.773
A horse walks into rehab.

00:11:41.960 --> 00:11:44.253
So why the long face?

00:11:45.240 --> 00:11:48.905
After five and a half seasons,
we're still finding out.

00:11:48.905 --> 00:11:52.072
(lighthearted music)

